{%- comment -%}
  fye-filter-icons — metal swatches and ring-profile shapes for the xCloud
  filter rail.

  Ported 31/08/2026 from live, where this ran as an inline <script> + <style>
  inside a custom-liquid block on templates/collection.json, gated on
  collection.handle == 'plain-wedding-rings'. Every part of that arrangement is
  something this theme forbids — inline script, a custom-CSS box, and markup
  living in a JSON template where nobody would look for it.

  HOW IT WORKS. xCloud renders the filter rail at runtime, so the icons cannot
  be rendered into it from Liquid. This snippet emits two things and no script:

    1. a hidden <svg> holding the two shared gradients, which must be IN THE
       DOCUMENT (not in the <template>) because cloned nodes reference them by
       url(#id) and a definition inside an inert template is not resolvable;
    2. a <template> of icons keyed by data-fic, matching xCloud's own
       data-filter-value strings EXACTLY, including capitalisation.

  assets/fye-ui.js clones from the template into the rail as the app renders
  it. That is the only script involved, and it is the theme's one JS file.

  WHY THIS IS LEANER THAN LIVE. Live inlined a full <linearGradient> per icon —
  nineteen of them, with unique ids, inside JSON-escaped strings inside a
  Liquid setting inside a template file. Two shared defs replace all nineteen,
  the colours are core tokens rather than repeated hexes, and the markup is
  real markup rather than an escaped string, so it cannot rot from a bad
  backslash.

  THE VALUE STRINGS ARE THE CONTRACT. If a filter value is renamed in Shopify
  or in xCloud, its icon silently stops appearing — no error, just a plain row.
  That is the intended failure: a missing icon is survivable, a broken rail is
  not. When adding a metal or a profile, copy the label from the rail itself.
{%- endcomment -%}

<svg class="fic-defs" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" role="presentation">
  <defs>
    <linearGradient id="fic-sheen" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1">
      <stop offset="0" stop-color="var(--metal-sheen-hi)"></stop>
      <stop offset="0.5" stop-color="var(--metal-sheen-mid)"></stop>
      <stop offset="1" stop-color="var(--metal-sheen-lo)"></stop>
    </linearGradient>
    <linearGradient id="fic-band" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
      <stop offset="0" stop-color="var(--metal-band-hi)"></stop>
      <stop offset="1" stop-color="var(--metal-band-lo)"></stop>
    </linearGradient>
  </defs>
</svg>

